# HY200 QZ713DF A1 -- one board, two stock firmwares. The silkscreen of cstenger's bench board (the
# mainline port's bring-up board), of the "HY300 Pro+" of 2025 (DDR3) and of the maintainer's
# HY300PRO-G-EU (read off the board, 02.10.2026). Old names: BOARD=ddr3 (build/build.sh alias) and
# boards/hy300pro-g-eu (until ST3-BOARDMERGE). README.md compares the two, row by row.
BOARD_ID=hy200-qz713df-a1
# The firmware a unit left the factory with is a variant: variants/<stock build>/variant.env, read
# after this file, its keys win. release/build-all.sh needs --variant for this board.
VARIANTS="projector05061226 projector09220931"
# The board as a whole; each variant states its own STATUS, VERIFIED_BY and IMAGE_NAME. Nobody has
# reported a green run of ours on any unit (cstenger's runs are his own tree's, on his bench).
STATUS=profile-only
VERIFIED_BY=
PROFILE=hy200_qz713df_a1
IMAGE_NAME=h713-hy200-qz713df-a1
# kernel patch 0181: the tree measured on the HY300PRO-G-EU (0167) under the board's name - lamp
# PWM words, fan tacho PH13, no pwm-backlight, no focus motor. Both firmwares' stock trees agree
# on all of it except the focus motor (README.md).
KERNEL_DTB=sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1
# U-Boot base hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig: layout v4, the board's DRAM words at 624 MHz; a variant's
# DRAM_CLK goes over it (build/uboot-build.sh).
UBOOT_BOARD=hy200_qz713df_a1
# Optional hardware (boards/README.md, FEATURES): none confirmed for every unit of the board; a
# variant names what was measured on its unit.
FEATURES=
# crust, our ARISC firmware (release/build-all.sh step 1b), for the whole board as its device tree names it
# (kernel 0246): the HY310's self-refresh build with this board's id. The DRAM words it uses are the HY310's at
# 792 MHz, projector05061226's clock; projector09220931 runs at 624 MHz and needs its own config before it is
# offered a standby (crust uses the clock only there). Measured on projector05061226 on 10.10.2026 (doku/184).
CRUST_DEFCONFIG=h713_hy200_qz713df_a1_sr_defconfig
